# A pop is written out. The kind of storage is loaded and compared, first with integers: that arm loads the last element, stores the mark of a hole over it and stores the shorter length.
# LOOP-LABEL: loop #
# LOOP: Int32 b@[[kind]] = Load8Z(b@{{*}}, offset = 4, ControlDependent|Reads:JSArray_indexingTypeAndMisc)
# LOOP: Int32 b@[[isIntegers]] = Equal(b@[[kind]], $5(b@{{*}}))
# LOOP: Branch(b@[[isIntegers]], Terminal)
# LOOP: Int64 b@{{*}} = Load(b@{{*}}, offset = -8, ControlDependent|Reads:indexedInt32Properties)
# LOOP: Store($0(b@{{*}}), b@{{*}}, offset = -8, ControlDependent|Writes:indexedInt32Properties)
# LOOP: Store(b@{{*}}, b@{{*}}, offset = -8, ControlDependent|Writes:Butterfly_publicLength)
# The arms for doubles and for any values follow, each behind one more comparison of the same byte.
# LOOP: Int32 b@{{*}} = Equal(b@[[kind]], $7(b@{{*}}))
# LOOP: Double b@{{*}} = Load(b@{{*}}, offset = -8, ControlDependent|Reads:indexedDoubleProperties)
# LOOP: Int32 b@{{*}} = Equal(b@[[kind]], $9(b@{{*}}))
# LOOP: Int64 b@{{*}} = Load(b@{{*}}, offset = -8, ControlDependent|Reads:indexedContiguousProperties)
# LOOP-LABEL: end of loop
# Only a list in none of the three kinds of storage calls Array.prototype.pop itself: the one call in the loop beside the poll. The kind is loaded once a turn.
# CALLS-LABEL: loop #
# CALLS-COUNT-1: Reads:JSArray_indexingTypeAndMisc
# CALLS-NOT: Reads:JSArray_indexingTypeAndMisc
# CALLS: isLoopPoll, ExitsSideways
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
# CALLS: ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallBuiltin)
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-LABEL: end of loop
# The counts hold a call, whose moves follow the calling convention: not for Windows.
